# Code owners for security-sensitive paths.
#
# Why: this is a public community repo. A normal app submission ONLY touches
# apps/<slug>/ (app.yaml + logo.png). Anything below runs in CI or affects the
# build/deploy — a "submission" PR that edits these is a red flag. Requiring a
# maintainer (code owner) review on these paths is a tripwire against a PR that
# sneaks in a malicious workflow / script / dependency.
#
# Enforced only when branch protection has "Require review from Code Owners"
# enabled for main. apps/** is intentionally NOT listed — that is the free
# contribution zone (still gated by the manual-approval ruleset, just not by
# code-owner review).

# CI / automation (workflows, this file, PR & issue templates)
/.github/            @celeste1900 @larrykoo711

# Build & validation scripts that run in CI
/scripts/            @celeste1900 @larrykoo711

# Dependencies (npm ci runs lifecycle scripts) and build/deploy config
/package.json        @celeste1900 @larrykoo711
/package-lock.json   @celeste1900 @larrykoo711
/astro.config.mjs    @celeste1900 @larrykoo711
/vercel.json         @celeste1900 @larrykoo711
/tsconfig.json       @celeste1900 @larrykoo711

# Submission schema (defines what app.yaml is allowed to contain)
/schema/             @celeste1900 @larrykoo711
